@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:architecture] lingui-macros-compiled
Every platform webpack config MUST run `linguiMacroLoader` (`config/webpack_lingui.ts`) on `.ts` and
`.tsx` sources, including the `front` ones, before `ts-loader`, and MUST load `.catalog` imports with
`linguiCatalogRule`. The bundle MUST NOT contain a `@lingui/*/macro` module.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:react] app-root-provides-i18n
Each platform app root (`ChromeApp`, `FirefoxApp`, `FrontApp`) MUST render its whole tree inside an
`I18nProvider` given the `i18n` instance of `@app/lib/i18n/i18n`, then inside a
`SparkleLocaleProvider`, so that shared `front` and sparkle components render in the locale that
`UserLocaleSync` activates, and in `DEFAULT_LOCALE` before it activates one.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:architecture] extension-strings-in-own-catalog
User-visible strings of extension sources MUST be translated with Lingui macros and extracted into
the single extension catalog of `lingui.config.ts` (`extension/locales/{locale}/messages.po`).
Code that cannot use `t` of `useLingui` MUST translate them by passing a `msg` descriptor to `i18n._`
of `@app/lib/i18n/i18n`, never with the global `t` of `@lingui/core/macro`: it binds to the
`@lingui/core` copy resolved from `extension/`, which is never activated.
